abstract: >-
  Telemetry and analysis pipeline behind a longitudinal study of
  large language model inference on a CPU-only edge node. Four
  architecturally distinct models (Qwen2.5 0.5B, Phi-3 Mini,
  Llama 3.1 8B, DeepSeek-v2 Lite) were each held under continuous
  inference for 48 hours across six CPU frequency-capping
  scenarios, totalling 1,152 hours of load, 296,064 inference
  events and 4.8 million out-of-band wall-plug power samples.
  The repository contains the raw per-campaign streams, the fusion
  and analysis code, and a manifest recording which campaigns feed
  the reported results and why the others do not.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - edge computing
  - energy efficiency
  - software aging
  - frequency scaling
  - carbon-aware computing
  - sustained inference
# Two licences apply: MIT covers src/, scripts/, analysis_output/ and the
# documentation; CC-BY-4.0 covers the measurement data under logs/. Anyone
# reusing the data owes attribution, which a bare "MIT" here would hide.
license:
